[*]Common tree (L4 II + L5 II): [URL="https://github.com/chijure-android-system-development/android_device_lge_mt6575-common"]android_device_lge_mt6575-common[/URL] (branch jellybean)
[*]Vendor blobs: [URL="https://github.com/chijure-android-system-development/android_vendor_lge_vee4ss"]android_vendor_lge_vee4ss[/URL], from the stock E440g firmware (the Bluetooth app comes from the E450g's)
[*]Kernel: stock prebuilt (MT6575, Linux 3.4)
[*]Base: CyanogenMod 10 (Android 4.1.2); the few platform changes still needed are kept as patches in mt6575-common/patches
[/LIST]

[B]Changelog[/B]

[B]2026-10-25 — Build 3[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]The zip flashes the boot image itself[/B], in MediaTek format. No more dd from the TWRP shell.
[*][B]Audio fixed[/B] through a wrapper around the stock audio HAL (output and microphone).
[*][B]Camera and video recording fixed[/B]: recording no longer stops after a few seconds, and recorded videos have correct colors. Camera controls resized for the 320×480 screen.
[*][B]Telephony working[/B]: calls, SMS and mobile data, tested with Entel. The RIL wrapper accepts incoming calls (before, they never rang), attaches to GPRS when the radio turns on, and reports call progress so the call screen follows the call. rild no longer crashes; IMEI and baseband come up.
[*]APNs for Claro, Movistar and Entel Peru; SIM Toolkit added.
[*][B]Bluetooth[/B]: LG's stock MediaTek Bluetooth app replaces CyanogenMod's, which could not open connections on this stack. Pairings are now saved and Bluetooth turns itself back on after a reboot.
[*][B]Home key LED[/B]: same behavior as LG's stock service (boot pattern, charging/full patterns with the screen off).
[*][B]Video[/B]: MediaTek hardware codecs. Recording is MPEG-4 640×480 with AAC (was 320×240 software encoding); H.264 Main/High videos now play. Fixed H.264 videos standing still or skipping: the MediaTek decoder drops the frame timestamps, the codec wrapper now restores them.
[*]Each phone shows up in adb with its own serial (codename plus eMMC serial) instead of 0123456789ABCDEF.
[*]Proximity sensor confirmed working; USB defaults to MTP.
[*]The L4 II and L5 II now share the mt6575-common tree.
[/LIST]

[B]2026-07-30 — Build 2[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Camera recording crashes fixed; first working audio (stock audio HAL module id issue).
[/LIST]

[B]2026-07-29 — Build 1 (initial public test)[/B]
[LIST]
[*]First build with a working display on this phone (MediaTek HWC/GraphicBuffer extensions); Bluetooth stack brought up.
[/LIST]

